Converted tasks
---------------

The task packs under conversions/terminal-bench/ and conversions/deep-swe/
are modified versions of tasks from two benchmarks, both released under the
Apache License, Version 2.0:

- Terminal-Bench 2
  https://github.com/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2
  commit 2fd12b88aafdd04a52c298e3940bcb189f9766d6

- DeepSWE
  https://github.com/datacurve-ai/deep-swe
  commit e016041a6ccf8da29906afc9a3f5a8df940a1f78

Each pack's CONVERSION.md states how the pack differs from its upstream task.

Third-party material inside the packs and results
-------------------------------------------------

The upstream tasks contain code, tests and data from third-party projects.
The packs carry that material over, and the stored candidates under runs/
contain agents' changes to it. Each project keeps its own license. In
particular:

- conversions/terminal-bench/adaptive-rejection-sampler/task/evaluation/r.tar.xz
  holds the files that Debian's r-base-core 4.3.3 package and its
  dependencies install. R is licensed under the GNU General Public License,
  version 2 or later. The source is available from Debian and from
  https://www.r-project.org/.

- conversions/terminal-bench/headless-terminal/task/evaluation/vim/ holds
  Debian packages of Vim and its dependencies, unmodified. Each package
  carries its own copyright file. The source is available from Debian.

- conversions/terminal-bench/train-fasttext/task/evaluation/reviews.txt.gz
  holds review texts taken from the test archive that the upstream task
  distributes.

Documentation copies
--------------------

adversarial/native-docs/ holds copies of public documentation of the Harbor
task format and of the Pier README. The native adversarial campaign gave
these files to its agents. They belong to their respective authors.
